    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong>Table&nbsp;3.05</strong> Immunohistochemical markers for the most common metastatic carcinomas to bone: primary site determination</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Jason L. Hornick",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"width: 22.0cm; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Primary site</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong>CK7 and CK20<br />(most-common patterns)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 361.45pt; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: none; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"482\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong>Other markers</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.0pt; border: none; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"217\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong>Cytoplasmic or membranous</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 7.0cm; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong>Nuclear<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Breast</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">CK7+, CK20&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"217\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">GCDFP-15, mammaglobin</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 7.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">ER, GATA3, SOX10 (triple-negative)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Kidney (renal cell carcinoma)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">CK7&minus;, CK20&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"217\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">RCCm</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 7.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">PAX8</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Liver (hepatocellular carcinoma)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">CK7&minus;, CK20&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"217\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Arginase-1 (ARG1), CPS1 (Hep&nbsp;Par-1)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 7.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Arginase-1 (ARG1)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Lung (adenocarcinoma)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">CK7+, CK20&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"217\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Napsin&nbsp;A</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 7.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">TTF1</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Pancreas</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">CK7+, CK20&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"217\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 7.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">SMAD4 (loss)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Prostate</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">CK7&minus;, CK20&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"217\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">PSA, PSAP</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 7.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">NKX3-1</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Small cell carcinoma<sup>b</sup></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"217\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Chromogranin, synaptophysin</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 7.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">TTF1, RB1 (loss)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Squamous cell carcinoma<sup>c</sup></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"217\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">High-molecular-weight cytokeratins (e.g. CK5)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 7.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">p63, p40</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Thyroid</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">CK7+, CK20&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.0pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"217\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Thyroglobulin</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 7.0cm; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">PAX8, TTF1</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>Nuclear markers are particularly susceptible to decalcification; the possibility of false-negative results (when relevant) should be included in a disclaimer in pathology reports. <sup>b</sup>Immunohistochemistry cannot distinguish among metastatic small cell carcinomas (i.e. pulmonary vs extrapulmonary origin). <sup>c</sup>Immunohistochemistry cannot distinguish among metastatic squamous cell carcinomas (other than p16&nbsp;&ndash; diffuse staining suggests a high-risk HPV&ndash;associated squamous cell carcinoma, such as from the oropharynx, anal canal, or uterine cervix).</p>",
